    "goal": "Make every production reader of a declared lane document take its headroom from reckon.crew.lane_document (the gate-aware reader landed at 08fc92c6), so flight's _probe_lane_document in reckon/flight.py (about line 1045) and dispatch's lane-document carry in reckon/crew/dispatch.py (about line 2315) report the same admission-limited headroom as crew(view=lanes), not the engine figure they parse themselves today. The published lane.json now carries admission.{headroom, verdict (congested/full/open/paused), waiting, oldest_wait_seconds}, a top-level headroom equal to min(engine, admission), and engine_headroom. The reader must prefer admission.* whenever present and fall back to computing from the router gate otherwise. Also repair lane_document.py around line 189, where the if and else arms assign an identical reason string, so an open gate and a congested gate give distinct reasons. Review finding being answered: paired readings of the live document minutes apart gave gate-aware 7, flight probe 12, dispatch carry 12.",
